\begin{align*}
\bullet&\ \text { gold or purple } \\
\bullet&\ \text { gold } \\
\bullet&\ \text { purple }
\end{align*}
For the first sub-rectangle, there are three options. However, from the second and third, there are two, as we cannot use gold twice (as we cannot start with purple). Therefore, by the product rule there are $3 \times 2 \times 2=\boxed{\textbf{(A)}~12.}$</think>
